166
00:10:02.852 --> 00:10:05.711
Run-once coordination: leases and fencing.

167
00:10:05.991 --> 00:10:10.876
Every lock with a timeout is a lease: it expires whether or not the holder is finished.

168
00:10:11.156 --> 00:10:17.769
A process can pause (GC, VM steal, a slow disk) past its lease and then act as if it still holds it.

