215
00:11:34.893 --> 00:11:39.224
Plain DEL deletes whatever lock is there, including the next holder's.

216
00:11:39.504 --> 00:11:44.283
That caused more runs (114 for 100 ticks) and more overlap.

217
00:11:44.563 --> 00:11:51.432
An owner token (compare-and-delete in Lua) stops that, but a paused holder still wakes up and writes its stale batch.

218
00:11:51.712 --> 00:11:59.477
Fencing tokens: a monotonically increasing number issued with each lease (Redis INCR, etcd revision, ZooKeeper zxid).

219
00:11:59.757 --> 00:12:03.427
The resource rejects anything older than the newest it has seen.

220
00:12:04.777 --> 00:12:06.483
Check the token on the read too.

221
00:12:06.763 --> 00:12:12.929
A first version of L1 checked the token only on the write, and still duplicated 100 events.

222
00:12:13.209 --> 00:12:18.947
The new holder had read the cursor before the old holder's late (and still-valid-looking) write landed.

223
00:12:19.227 --> 00:12:23.281
The fix is to claim the row with your token before reading it (UPDATE...

224
00:12:23.561 --> 00:12:30.387
SET fence = token WHERE fence token RETURNING pos), then write only while the fence is still yours.

225
00:12:30.667 --> 00:12:31.691
Alternatives:

226
00:12:31.971 --> 00:12:36.003
Make the effect idempotent (a unique key per event or per period).

227
00:12:37.353 --> 00:12:43.540
Use a single-writer design, such as a Kafka partition owner with epoch fencing (Ch 14).

228
00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.044
Keep the lease in the same database as the effect, for example, SELECT...

229
00:12:48.324 --> 00:12:51.183
FOR UPDATE on a job row held for the transaction.

230
00:12:51.463 --> 00:13:04.433
Where leases live: etcd or ZooKeeper (consensus-backed, with revisions as tokens), the database (row leases), or Redis (fast, but a single primary; Redlock's guarantees are debated, Ch 12).

231
00:13:05.783 --> 00:13:07.810
Storing and firing delayed jobs.

232
00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:13.295
A durable store holds (id, dueat, status, leaseuntil, attempts, payload, tenant).

233
00:13:13.575 --> 00:13:17.245
Workers find due jobs, lease them, run them, and mark them done.

