411
00:22:04.358 --> 00:22:07.451
FIFO turns one tenant's dump into everyone's outage.

412
00:22:07.731 --> 00:22:15.667
Priority classes protect against bulk, but a flood inside a class (the payments bug) hurts every tenant in that class and below.

413
00:22:15.947 --> 00:22:21.110
Fair queuing (deficit round robin, weighted fair queuing) isolates tenants from each other.

414
00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:26.894
It doesn't isolate a tenant from itself: payments' fresh checks waited behind its own retries.

415
00:22:27.174 --> 00:22:36.945
Retry lanes (separate queues for retries, as in Ch 40), weights, per-tenant concurrency caps and quotas keep first attempts fast while floods drain.

416
00:22:38.295 --> 00:22:46.721
Admission control: reject or defer at enqueue when a tenant exceeds its quota, and tell the producer (Ch 46 waiting room).

417
00:22:47.001 --> 00:22:53.508
Physical isolation for the most critical work: separate worker pools (a cell or bulkhead, Ch 18).

418
00:22:54.858 --> 00:22:56.330
Execution semantics.

419
00:22:56.610 --> 00:23:05.591
At-least-once is the practical default: a job may run again after a lease expiry, a crash, or a timeout followed by a late completion.

420
00:23:05.871 --> 00:23:17.285
Jobs must be idempotent (keys per logical run, for example, settlement:2026 to 09 to 29T18), or fenced (§2.4).

421
00:23:17.565 --> 00:23:20.317
Timeouts: a heartbeat extends the lease while working.

422
00:23:20.597 --> 00:23:24.245
Without heartbeats, the lease must exceed the worst-case duration.

423
00:23:24.525 --> 00:23:30.327
Retries: exponential backoff with jitter, a max attempt count, then dead-letter with alerting.

424
00:23:30.607 --> 00:23:33.381
Distinguish retryable errors from permanent ones.

425
00:23:34.731 --> 00:23:36.587
Cancellation: cooperative.

426
00:23:36.867 --> 00:23:40.941
The job checks a flag, or checks its fencing token at its next step.

427
00:23:42.291 --> 00:23:43.422
