00:28:49.408 --> 00:28:50.816
Decisions in detail.

500
00:28:52.166 --> 00:28:54.577
Leases (ADR-360).

501
00:28:54.857 --> 00:29:00.361
Each job shard is a lease in etcd with TTL 10 s and heartbeats every 3 s.

502
00:29:00.641 --> 00:29:05.803
The revision is passed to handlers as the fencing token, and handlers write fence columns.

503
00:29:06.083 --> 00:29:08.665
Storage (ADR-361).

504
00:29:08.945 --> 00:29:10.182
Hourly partitions.

505
00:29:10.462 --> 00:29:13.705
Loaders own shards hash(id) % 64.

506
00:29:13.985 --> 00:29:16.651
Batches are written back every 100 ms.

507
00:29:16.931 --> 00:29:19.427
Bursts (ADR-362).

508
00:29:19.707 --> 00:29:24.337
Producers declare jitter tolerance, and the API spreads due times within it.

509
00:29:24.617 --> 00:29:26.814
DAGs (ADR-363).

510
00:29:27.094 --> 00:29:29.462
Tasks are idempotent by logical date.

511
00:29:29.742 --> 00:29:34.862
SLAs are defined per DAG, with early alerts from critical-path projections.

512
00:29:36.212 --> 00:29:38.879
Fairness (ADR-364).

513
00:29:39.159 --> 00:29:41.740
Quotas per tenant in worker-seconds per minute.

514
00:29:42.020 --> 00:29:44.068
Excess is deferred, not dropped.

515
00:29:44.348 --> 00:29:45.372
Consequences.

516
00:29:45.652 --> 00:29:52.095
Costs: etcd operations, partition management, a DAG engine to run, and tenant quota governance.

517
00:29:52.375 --> 00:29:59.585
Benefits: single-effect singletons, on-time firing at bursts, correct nightly pipelines, and tenant isolation.

518
