634
00:42:10.673 --> 00:42:11.953
Production Concerns.

635
00:42:13.203 --> 00:42:14.355
Failure modes.

636
00:42:14.635 --> 00:42:15.979
Here is a quick table:

637
00:42:16.259 --> 00:42:18.541
Failure, and Symptom, and Mitigation.

638
00:42:18.821 --> 00:42:20.379
Scheduler on every pod.

639
00:42:20.659 --> 00:42:21.469
Symptom:

640
00:42:21.749 --> 00:42:23.456
N executions (L1).

641
00:42:23.736 --> 00:42:24.739
Mitigation:

642
00:42:25.019 --> 00:42:25.915
Leases.

643
00:42:26.195 --> 00:42:27.517
Lock without fencing.

644
00:42:27.797 --> 00:42:28.608
Symptom:

645
00:42:28.888 --> 00:42:31.384
Duplicate effects after pauses (L1).

646
00:42:31.664 --> 00:42:32.667
Mitigation:

647
00:42:32.947 --> 00:42:36.104
Fencing tokens on read and write; idempotency.

648
00:42:36.384 --> 00:42:37.813
Plain DEL release.

649
00:42:38.093 --> 00:42:38.904
Symptom:

650
00:42:39.184 --> 00:42:41.488
Deletes the next holder's lock (L1).

651
00:42:41.768 --> 00:42:42.771
Mitigation:

652
00:42:43.051 --> 00:42:44.267
Owner-checked release.

653
00:42:44.547 --> 00:42:45.528
Tight polling.

654
00:42:45.808 --> 00:42:46.619
Symptom:

655
00:42:46.899 --> 00:42:48.968
DB load, still late (L2).

656
00:42:49.248 --> 00:42:50.251
Mitigation:

657
00:42:50.531 --> 00:42:51.960
Lookahead + timers.

658
00:42:52.240 --> 00:42:53.413
Queue table churn.

659
00:42:53.693 --> 00:42:54.504
Symptom:

660
00:42:54.784 --> 00:42:56.619
Slow claims, bloat (L2).

661
00:42:56.899 --> 00:42:57.901
Mitigation:

662
00:42:58.181 --> 00:43:00.955
Partitioning, history tables, vacuum tuning.

663
00:43:01.235 --> 00:43:02.536
Round-time bursts.

664
00:43:02.816 --> 00:43:03.627
Symptom:

665
00:43:03.907 --> 00:43:07.235
Late jobs at 18:00:00.

666
00:43:07.515 --> 00:43:08.517
Mitigation:

667
00:43:08.797 --> 00:43:11.059
Batch claims, parallel fire, jitter.

668
00:43:11.339 --> 00:43:12.384
Cron chaining.

669
00:43:12.664 --> 00:43:13.475
Symptom:

670
00:43:13.755 --> 00:43:16.080
Wrong reports on slow nights (L3).

671
00:43:16.360 --> 00:43:17.363
Mitigation:

672
00:43:17.643 --> 00:43:19.819
DAG dependencies, retries.

673
00:43:21.169 --> 00:43:22.193
Shared FIFO.

674
00:43:22.473 --> 00:43:23.283
Symptom:

675
00:43:23.563 --> 00:43:25.569
Cross-tenant outages (L4).

676
00:43:25.849 --> 00:43:26.851
Mitigation:

677
00:43:27.131 --> 00:43:29.371
Fair queuing, retry lanes, quotas.

678
00:43:29.651 --> 00:43:31.209
Misfire after downtime.

679
00:43:31.489 --> 00:43:32.299
Symptom:

680
00:43:32.579 --> 00:43:34.009
Floods or missed runs.

681
00:43:34.289 --> 00:43:35.291
Mitigation:

682
00:43:35.571 --> 00:43:37.299
Per-job misfire policy.

683
00:43:38.649 --> 00:43:39.737
Observability.

684
00:43:40.017 --> 00:43:44.647
Lateness (start minus due) per tenant and job type; backlog by due time.

685
00:43:44.927 --> 00:43:50.025
Lease churn, fenced writes (should be rare but non-zero), duplicate-effect detectors.

686
00:43:50.305 --> 00:43:57.495
DAG critical-path projection versus SLA (payouts projected 06:20), with early paging.

687
00:43:57.775 --> 00:44:03.684
Per-tenant queue depth, wait p99, worker-seconds used versus quota; dead-letter counts.

688
00:44:03.964 --> 00:44:08.017
Run history with inputs and logs; searchable by logical date.

689
00:44:09.367 --> 00:44:10.306
Security.

690
00:44:10.586 --> 00:44:15.343
Jobs run with the tenant's service identity, not the scheduler's; least privilege.

691
00:44:15.623 --> 00:44:21.234
Payloads carry references, not secrets; secrets come from the vault at execution time.

692
00:44:21.514 --> 00:44:26.378
Manual re-runs and backfills are audited, and need approval for financial jobs.

693
00:44:27.728 --> 00:44:28.624
Performance.

694
00:44:28.904 --> 00:44:32.168
Batch everything: claims, write-backs, history inserts.

695
00:44:32.448 --> 00:44:35.093
Timing wheels for millions of in-memory timers.

696
00:44:35.373 --> 00:44:39.000
Shard loaders by partition; scale workers per tenant lane.

697
00:44:40.350 --> 00:44:41.075
Cost.

698
00:44:41.355 --> 00:44:42.678
Workers are the cost.

699
00:44:42.958 --> 00:44:45.838
Quotas and weights turn contention into policy.

700
00:44:46.118 --> 00:44:50.875
Partition dropping is far cheaper than DELETE and VACUUM on hot queue tables.

701
00:44:51.155 --> 00:44:57.065
Heavy nights need extra slots: autoscale the DAG workers on the critical-path projection.

702
00:44:58.415 --> 00:44:59.353
